## QUESTION : KYA USERS BADHNE KA MATLAB HAMESHA SCALING ZARURI HAI ?
------------------------------------------------------------------------

NAHI.

Example:

    Total Users         = 1000
    Concurrent Users    = 10

Scaling required?

Maybe not.

Kyunki actual load total users se nahi, concurrent users se decide hota hai.



----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
## QUESTION : AGAR CPU 100% HAI, TO KYA SCALING SE PROBLEM HAMESHA SOLVE HO JAYEGI ?
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Suppose application me infinite loop likh diya.

CPU 100%.

Sawaal: Scaling se problem solve hogi?

Answer: NO.

Kyunki scaling se capacity badhti hai, code bug fix nahi hota.

Agar infinite loop hai, to naye servers par bhi wahi infinite loop chalega,
aur CPU wahan bhi 100% ho jayega. Resources waste honge.

Pehle bug fix karna padega.

Root cause identify karo:
    - Application logs
    - Thread dumps

Uske baad scaling ka socho.



----------------------------------------------------------------------
## QUESTION : SABSE PEHLE KAUNSA RESOURCE BOTTLENECK BANTA HAI ?
----------------------------------------------------------------------

Ye application par depend karta hai.

Examples:

CPU-intensive application
→ CPU

Database-heavy application
→ DB

Large File Upload
→ Network

Memory-intensive application
→ RAM

Iska koi universal answer nahi hai.



--------------------------------------------------------
## QUESTION : KYA HIGH CPU HAMESHA BURI BAAT HAI ?
--------------------------------------------------------

NAHI.

CPU 80–90% tak normal ho sakta hai.

Kyunki agar application expectedly CPU-intensive hai
(jaise video encoding, data processing, complex calculations),
to high CPU utilization normal hai.

Problem tab hai jab:

    - Response Time badh raha ho
    - Requests queue me wait kar rahi ho
    - Error Rate badh raha ho

Isliye CPU utilization alone decision nahi hota.







-------------------------------------------------
## HOW CAN WE HANDLE THE INCREASED WORKLOAD ?
-------------------------------------------------

Ab tak humne dekha ki jaise-jaise application par traffic increase hota gaya,
ek single server ke limited resources gradually exhaust hone lage.

Result:

        Existing Workload

                >

        Server Capacity


Question:

Ab company ke paas kya options hain?

Generally do approaches available hoti hain.


## OPTION-1
------------

Existing server ke Hardware Resources ko increase kar do.

Example:

CPU

    2 Cores

        ↓

    16 Cores

RAM

    4 GB

        ↓

    64 GB

Network

    1 Gbps

        ↓

    10 Gbps

Yaani existing machine ko aur powerful bana diya.

Is approach ko

    Vertical Scaling (Scale Up)

kehte hain.



## OPTION-2
------------

Ek hi powerful server ko continuously upgrade karne ke bajay,

application ke multiple instances different servers par deploy kar diye jaate hain.

Example:

Initially

                Users
                  |
                  |
                  v
            ----------------
            | Spring Boot  |
            | Application  |
            ----------------
                  |
                  v
               Database



After Scaling

                   Users
                      |
                      |
                      v
               Load Balancer
              /      |      \
             /       |       \
            v        v        v

      SpringBoot SpringBoot SpringBoot
        Server-1   Server-2   Server-3
             \        |        /
              \       |       /
               --------|-------
                      |
                  Database


Load Balancer incoming requests ko available application
instances ke beech distribute karta hai.

Is approach ko

    Horizontal Scaling (Scale Out)

kehte hain.


## WHICH APPROACH SHOULD WE CHOOSE ?
--------------------------------------

Is question ka koi universal answer nahi hai.

Ye mainly following factors par depend karta hai:

1. CURRENT TRAFFIC
-------------------
Agar traffic abhi kam hai, to Vertical Scaling sufficient ho sakti hai.
Agar traffic bahut zyada hai, to Horizontal Scaling ki zarurat pad sakti hai.


2. FUTURE TRAFFIC GROWTH
--------------------------
Agar expected hai ki users continuously increase honge,
to Horizontal Scaling generally better option hoti hai.


3. DOWNTIME TOLERANCE
-----------------------
Agar application ko server upgrade ke time kuch downtime allow hai,
to Vertical Scaling consider ki ja sakti hai.

Agar application ko continuously available rakhna hai,
to Horizontal Scaling generally preferred hoti hai.


4. BUDGET
-----------
Kabhi-kabhi ek powerful server lena sasta pad sakta hai.

Kabhi multiple normal servers use karna better option hota hai.

Ye infrastructure cost par depend karta hai.


5. APPLICATION ARCHITECTURE
-----------------------------

Kuch applications ko horizontally scale karna relatively easy hota hai.

Kuch applications ko horizontally scale karne ke liye additional changes karne padte hain.


## WHY DOES THIS CREATE A PROBLEM IN HORIZONTAL SCALING?
---------------------------------------------------------

Horizontal Scaling sirf multiple application instances
deploy kar dene se complete nahi ho jaati.

Suppose application ke multiple instances chal rahe hain.

                   Load Balancer
                  /      |      \
                 /       |       \
                v        v        v

            Server-1  Server-2  Server-3

User ne login kiya.

Load Balancer ne login request

    Server-1

par bhej di.

Server-1 ne HttpSession create ki aur
user ka login session apni local memory (RAM)
me store kar diya.

Ab user ki next request aayi.

Is baar Load Balancer ne request

    Server-2

ko forward kar di.

Problem:

Server-2 ke paas Server-1 wali HttpSession
available hi nahi hai,

kyunki wo sirf Server-1 ki local memory
me stored thi.

Result:

Server-2 ko lagega ki user login hi nahi hai.

User ko dobara login karna pad sakta hai,
ya request fail ho sakti hai (application implementation par depend karta hai).

Isi wajah se Horizontal Scaling ke liye
sirf multiple application instances deploy
kar dena enough nahi hota.

Application ko bhi horizontally scalable
banana padta hai.

Common Solutions:

    - Stateless Design (Most Preferred)
    - External Session Store (Redis)
    - Sticky Sessions (Less Preferred)


6. HIGH AVAILABILITY REQUIREMENT
---------------------------------
Agar ek server fail hone ke baad bhi application continuously
chalti rehni chahiye, to Horizontal Scaling generally better choice hoti hai.



## CAN BOTH APPROACHES BE USED TOGETHER ?
-------------------------------------------

Yes.

Production systems me sirf Vertical ya sirf Horizontal
Scaling use karna mandatory nahi hai.

Bahut saari companies dono approaches ka combination
use karti hain.

Example:

Pehle server ko reasonably powerful banaya jaata hai
(Vertical Scaling).

Uske baad traffic aur increase hone par multiple
application instances deploy karke Horizontal Scaling
ki jaati hai.

Yaani,

        Vertical Scaling

                +

        Horizontal Scaling

ka combination bhi production environments me
kaafi common hai.


## NOTE:
---------

Horizontal Scaling primarily increases the capacity of the application tier.
As traffic grows further, the database can also become a bottleneck and may need to be scaled.
Database Scaling is a separate topic and will be discussed later.
